e mercado o necesidades específicas.\nQué se puede revisar: Comprobar si los contratos [1], [2], [3] atienden la misma necesidad. Verificar si el adjudicatario A repite contratos en otros ámbitos. Analizar si los contratos al límite se distribuyen según criterios legales.","en":"What the data shows: Between 2023 and 2025, this body awarded 110 minor contracts for services and supplies above 14,000 and up to 15,000 euros, just under the legal limit. If those amounts were spread as in the band immediately below, 36.6 contracts would be expected. The observed-to-expected ratio is 3.0, with a 95% confidence interval of 2.4 to 3.8. December accounts for 8% of the contracts just under the limit, compared with 13% of all its services and supplies contracts. The awardee with the most contracts just under the limit, called awardee A here, has 7. Contract [1], for 14,450 euros, was awarded in December 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: The concentration of contracts near the legal limit does not prove misconduct. It could reflect market pricing, budget constraints, or separate needs. Statistical patterns alone do not indicate improper actions by any party.\nWhat can be checked: Check the distribution of contracts across different months and awardees. Review the specific services and supplies described in contract [1] to ensure they align with the body's needs. Verify if multiple contracts cover the same service to identify potential overlaps or redundancies.","origen_es":"modelo","origen_en":"modelo","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"ss","citas":["Y4rK081xqUW9Hd5zqvq9cg%3D%3D","%2FSGXIdBm395J8Trn0ZPzLw%3D%3D","F%2FIYsB5xxVTVGIpKDxgsAQ%3D%3D"],"generado":"2026-11-16"}}